      "title": "Water supply restored to Gatwick airport after hours without working toilets",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jul/26/water-supply-failure-gatwick-airport-toilets-bars-restaurants",
      "description": "<p>Airport’s bars and restaurants were also unable to serve drinks to passengers because of lack of running water</p><p>Water supply has been restored to most of Gatwick airport after passengers spent hours without access to working toilets, and bars and restaurants were closed.</p><p>Most toilets had reopened across both terminals on Sunday evening, with the remaining facilities, including bars and restaurants, expected to return to normal for the first of Monday’s flights.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/jul/26/water-supply-failure-gatwick-airport-toilets-bars-restaurants\">Continue reading...</a>",
